# Generated at ingestion time: convert_xlsx_to_csv() (etl/source_files.py)
# writes a derived .csv beside its source .xlsx, same stem. That's build
# output, not source data - the .xlsx is the tracked original. Listed
# explicitly by name rather than a blanket *.csv rule, so a genuine
# raw-CSV-only extract added later (no .xlsx counterpart) stays trackable
# instead of silently disappearing into this file.
